   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Observed on-ball coverage labels (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) from NBA matchup/PBP fields were labelled on only 14.9% (DET, 10 of 67 possessions) and 3.3% (ORL, 2 of 60) of possessions; switches_on was not populated. Verdict: failed_gate."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-096",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "A play-type classifier using the assisted flag, which exists only on makes, produced SPOT_UP 2.83 PPP with 100% makes. After rewriting, SPOT_UP was about 1.16 and TRANSITION about 1.20. The record is an engineering discovery that poisoned a simulation."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-063",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Holdout validation of pre-game play-type PPP ranking on 908 game-team rows from 454 games: median rho +0.539; 88.4% rho>0; 10.5% rho<0; median top-3 lift +0.4261 PPP. The record notes the top-3 lift partly reflects league-wide high-efficiency play types (CUT, PUTBACK, TRANSITION). This concerns play-type efficiency ranking, not counter lift."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-034",
   "status_as_recorded": "no result recorded",
   "finding": "Opponent-relative leverage sweep over 870 ordered team pairs: exploit available 33.3%, trap 23.3%, both 6.7%, neither 50.0%; median best edge 3.79%. The record notes edges depend only on the defense (e.g. DAL PNR +9.2% for every offense), so they are not matchup-specific. The record has no auto_outcome_status field; its verdict is descriptive."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-012",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "ORL-DET opponent-specific decomposition: all top openers were 'universal only' (opponent-specific share +1.4% to +6.9%); DET was within ±5% of league on all seeded play types. No opponent-specific edge was detected in either direction."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-058",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "2024-25 shot-level PNR share of half-court shots ranged from about 7.6% (OKC) to 13.8% (IND). Possession-level PNR rates were later calibrated to about 17.9–19.6%. The record states there is no pass/fail gate and the rates are a calibration input."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-020",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Falsification T3 on the playoff A1 sample: the in-game adapter PPP lift did not carry over to Game N+1 (no PPP lift, negative mix-carry). The record's auto_failure_mechanism is B_powered_null, but its sample_and_power is NOT_RECORDED."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-066",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Four playoff games: team-level PNR lifts were small (ORL vs DET PNR +1.2pp; POR vs SAS PNR -4.1pp). Player-channel lifts were large but on n of about 15–54, with helper-steal attribution issues and no holdout."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-067",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Raw TOV-force channel lifts shrank by about 50% or more under opponent re-route and counter adjustments (e.g. ORL +8.4pp to net +3.7pp), on 4 games and 8 offense-defense sides. The net lift is model-implied rather than observed in games."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-020",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Holdout evaluation on 520 matchup cells and 69,876 possessions: equilibrium R2 -0.1981, actual-mix R2 -0.7167, team-offense mean R2 +0.1197. The lambda sweep worsened R2 monotonically. Predictors built from matchup mixes did not beat simple team means."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058",
   "what_failed": "Labelling on-ball defensive coverage (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) from NBA matchup and PBP fields",
   "why": "Label rates were very low (14.9% and 3.3%), switches_on was unpopulated, and the record classes the failure as A_unanswerable with LABEL_ERROR and SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER risks."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-096",
   "what_failed": "Play-type inference that used the assisted flag",
   "why": "The assisted flag exists only on makes, which inflated SPOT_UP to 2.83 PPP. The record classes this as C_artifact. Play-type labels built from PBP can carry outcome-derived artifacts."
  },
