   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-066",
   "what_failed": "Player-channel decomposition of matchup lifts",
   "why": "Cell sizes of about 15–54 were too small, primary-defender attribution included helper steals, and there was no holdout. The record classes this as A_unanswerable with EXPOSURE_SPARSITY."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-067",
   "what_failed": "Counter-adjusted TOV-force lifts",
   "why": "Lifts shrank by about 50% or more after adjustment, and the net lift was model-implied, not observed. The record's mechanism is E_unclear and the verdict is descriptive."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-020",
   "what_failed": "Matchup-equilibrium and actual-mix predictors of matchup PPP",
   "why": "Both had negative R2 on 520 holdout cells, while the simple team-offense mean scored +0.1197. The record's verdict is tool_eval_fail."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-012",
   "what_failed": "Opponent-specific play-type edge hypothesis for ORL-DET",
   "why": "No opponent-specific edge was detected. Shares were +1.4% to +6.9%, and the record's mechanism is E_unclear."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Several earlier studies in this project found that matchup-level or channel-level lifts from play-by-play shrink substantially under adjustment or holdout, and that small cells are unstable.",
  "Play-type labels derived from PBP have a documented artifact history (assisted-flag leak), so PULL_UP and PNR-fail labels need validation before use.",
  "Coverage labels from the matchup feed were sparse, so a conditioning event defined from defensive scheme labels may not be observable at useful rates.",
  "A holdout validation of play-type efficiency ranking (FAM:SF-APPA-063) shows that play-type efficiency is partly predictable at the game-team level, but it does not test counters."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
